  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale:\nWe propose a region flows approach that models the function h(x) as a mixture of piecewise constant regions with optimal density distribution. The central idea is that the minimum overlap occurs when the function h(x) has regions of high density separated by at least the shift distance (1 unit) to minimize cross-overlap. This is an adaptation of the method used in solving compressions and packing problems, and will be more effective at escaping local optima than the parent code's coordinate descent by incorporating multiple candidates and iterative regional optimization.\n\nThe key innovations are:\n- Formulating the problem as a multiple of independently movable regions rather than individual grid points\n- Using continuous density variables for regions and mapping them to piecewise constants\n- Maintaining a set of active candidates through simulated annealing\n- Combining this with grid size adaptation for escaping local minima\n\n2. Mathematical specifications:\nLet [0,2] be divided into N regions. Each region i has:\n- Length L_i\n- Continuous density d_i (later discretized)\n- Optimal spacing between regions\n\nThe optimization problem is:\nmin_{regions} max_k \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx\nsubject to:\n\u222b h(x) dx = 1\n0 <= h(x) <= 1\nL_i >= \u03b4_min (minimum separation between regions)\n\nObjective transformation:\nDefine cost_i = \u222b_{region i} h(x) (1 - h(x + k)) dx for k=0,1\nThe goal is to find region configurations minimizing max(cost_i for all i, k)\n\nThe optimization variables are:\n1. Region boundaries (global optimization problem)\n2. Local densities (convex optimization per region)\n\n3. Implementation procedure:\n   a) Initialize:\n      - Start from `initial_h_values` (n=400) but divide into regions (default approx 20 regions)\n      - Convert continuous densities to piecewise constants\n      - Maintain a set of candidate solutions\n\n   b) Optimization loop:\n      while time < budget_s and no improvement:\n          i. Simulate annealing steps:\n               - Select a random region to modify\n               - Add random perturbation to:\n                  a) Region boundaries (maintaining separation constraint)\n                  b) Local densities (constrained to [0,1])\n               - Calculate new overlap integral using:\n                  C5_new = max_k integrate h_new(x)(1-h_new(x+k)) dx\n\n          ii. Accept the new configuration if:\n              - C5_new < best score OR\n              - Random acceptance with probability p = exp(-(C5_new - best_score)/T)\n\n          iii. Adaptively adjust temperature and time budget for each optimization stage.\n\n   c) Region boundary optimization:\n        For each candidate configuration:\n        - Formulate as continuous optimization problem:\n             minimize_{L_i} sum_i \u03c8_i(L_i) = penalty for overlapping regions + region scatter score\n             subject to \u2211 L_i = 2, L_i \u2265 \u03b4\n             where \u03b4 = minimum separation between active regions\n\n        Solve using scipy.optimize.minimize with bounds and constraints\n\n   d) Density optimization:\n        For each candidate after region optimization:\n        - Solve for densities d_i minimizing penalized overlap:\n             min_{d_i} \u2211_i [region_i_overlap_score(d_i)] \n             s.t. \u2211_i L_i * d_i = 1\n              0 \u2264 d_i \u2264 1\n\n        Use projected gradient method\n\n   e) Solution extraction:\n        After optimization, determine best candidate configuration\n        Convert continuous representation back to piecewise constant step function\n        Ensure gradient constraints (integral=1, 0<=h<=1) with closing adjustment\n\n   f) Detailed flow:\n\n        def simulate_annealing():\n            for iteration in range(max_iter):\n                T = initial_temp / (1 + rate * iteration)\n                select random_region()\n                perturb_region(attributes=['location', 'density', 'width'])\n                calculate_new_score()\n                if new_score < best_score OR accept(probability=T):\n                    update(best_score=new_score)\n                if iteration % checkpoint == 0:\n                    region_optimization()\n                    grid_size_adaptation()\n\n        def region_optimization():\n            transform_regions(regions, densities)\n            define_cost_function(cost_k for k=0,1)\n            minimize_cost_with_gradient()\n\n        def grid_size_adaptation():\n            reduce_regions(0.75*initial_regions) if C5_improvement > 3 else increase_regions()\n\n   g)_Base code helpers reused: compute_c5(), project_feasible(), build_correlation_cache()_\n\n   h) New helper functions:\n        - make_regions(count, total_length)\n        - check_region_overlap()\n        - optimize_densities(log_barrier=False)\n\n4. Search choices and variations:\n   a) Region count: adaptable (start with 3-8, max 30)\n   b) Perturbation types:\n        i. 50% internal (change L_i and \u03b4)\n        ii. 30% external (add/remove regions)\n        iii. 20% density-based (change d_i)\n   c) Optimization modes (when temperature falls):\n        i. Active mode (fine-tuning)\n        ii. Restorative mode (recover shape)\n        iii. Exploration mode (large steps)\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness:\n   a) Time allocation:\n        - 300s initial region adaptation\n        - 500s region optimization cycles\n        - 200s density optimization\n        - 300s checkpoint improvements\n   b) Summerizeannealing implementation with:\n        initial_temp = 1.0\n        rate = 0.0005 (cooling rate)\n        min_iter = 10000\n   c) Deadline check every 100 iterations\n   d) Fallback strategy: return nearest feasible candidate that satisfies 0<=h<=1 with integral 1\n\n6. Validation and return contract:\n   a) Feasibility checks:\n        - 0 <= all(h) <= 1\n        - abs(sum(h)*dx - 1) < 1e-3\n   b) Score validation:\n        - Clean evaluation using np.correlate()\n        - Grid conversion with exact integral preservation\n   c) Final steps:\n        - Re-evaluate candidate solution using exact compute_c5()\n        - Return best_h, best_c5, n_points\n        - Ensure output has n_points matching budget phase",
